  {
    "slug": "darktraveltales",
    "title": "#DarkTravelTales ",
    "subtitle": "",
    "client": "Reliance General Insurence",
    "studio": "OgilvyOne",
    "period": "2013-2017",
    "start": 2013,
    "categories": [
      "Brand",
      "Digital",
      "Campaign"
    ],
    "featured": true,
    "statement": "",
    "description": "#DarkTravelTales\nfor Reliance general insurance\n\nTravel Insurance, a product that most of us don’t take seriously. Why? Because why would we need it. Incidents do happen, but ‘nothing can ever go wrong with us’. This is how we think when it comes to insurance, we just assume it as a waste of money, and skip over the part where it could actually save the day for us. But deep down we all know how things can go wrong with us while travelling.\n\n#DarkTravelTales stems from this insight. A Twitter led campaign, it took the audience on a roller coaster ride to contribute to the scripting of a thriller, only to make them realize the importance of travel insurance. Apart from getting noticed, this campaign also led to the making of the world’s first Twitter-curated graphic novel. \n\n#DarkTravelTales #KyooriusAward  #ENVIES #ECHO International\n\nAwards: \nOgilvy’s Finest - Envies 2015\nKyoorius - Blue Elephant : Use of Social - 2016\nKyoorius - Blue Elephant : Direct Innovation - 2016\nECHO International Silver - Best use of Social Media - 2016",
    "cover": "media/projects/darktraveltales/dtt-thumb.jpg",
    "story": {
      "problem": "",
      "outcome": "",
      "context": "",
      "users": ""
    },
    "media": [
      {
        "id": "tyfmkenq",
        "src": "media/projects/darktraveltales/dtt-thumb.jpg",
