  {
    "slug": "dontemploylittleones",
    "title": "#DontEmployLittleOnes",
    "subtitle": "",
    "client": "Reliance general insurance",
    "studio": "OgilvyOne",
    "period": "",
    "start": null,
    "categories": [
      "Brand",
      "Digital",
      "Campaign"
    ],
    "featured": false,
    "statement": "",
    "description": "#DontEmployLittleOnes\nfor Reliance general insurance\n\nChild labour, it’s something that we all feel bad about. But this is all most of us do about it, ‘feel bad’. And as soon as the poor child gets out of our sight, the matter automatically gets resolved. But is this how things should be? The answer is no! \nThat’s why Reliance General Insurance joined hands with CRY, India’s largest Children’s NGO to raise awareness about the topic. To do so, we came up with a simple yet effective idea. We urged the people in the Twitter universe to tweet everything in upper case and end it with the hashtag #DONTEMPLOYLITTLEONES, making each tweet a statement against child labour. \n\nAnd the response – It was nothing less than overwhelming. ",
    "cover": "media/projects/dontemploylittleones/delo-copy.png",
    "story": {},
